# Cleanup

Your mission is to search for clear issues that need to be fixed. You are not supposed to fix hypothetical minor issues. Only make changes that would have a real-world impact.

## Guidelines

### What to fix
- Remove console.log
- Remove debug code
- Evaluate if code can be consolidated
- Remove code obviously not used
- Move in-line styles to StyleSheet
- Make sure we never use color literals
- Remove obvious over engineering
- Remove unecessary comments
- Make sure we check for null when necessary
- Make sure we use modern and safe TypeScript
- Make sure we have no code intended for web usage
- Make low effort but high impact changes if they are safe
- Remove accessibility code that is not used
- Make sure we do not use `any`
- Use layout constraint from [layout.ts](mdc:constants/layout.ts)
- Make sure we use colors from [Colors.ts](mdc:constants/Colors.ts)